Network & Infrastructure Isolation:
The agent requires access to a private internal API, a staging environment behind a VPN, or a dedicated enterprise deployment target (e.g., Devin Outposts).
Compute & Entitlement Caps:
The evaluation exceeds default monthly AI Compute Unit (ACU) limits, requiring tier upgrades, custom enterprise contract terms, or pay-as-you-go overrides.
Identity & Governance Constraints:
The evaluation requires enterprise SSO/SAML mapping, custom security profiles, or specific secrets management policies that non-admin evaluation users cannot approve alone.
Complex Architecture Decisions:
The autonomous agent correctly identifies architectural trade-offs (e.g., microservice refactoring vs. legacy monolith integration) that require human strategic alignment rather than autonomous code generation.
When these boundaries are reached, the user experiences a hard stop. Without immediate intervention, the evaluation cold-starts, context is lost, and the probability of closing the enterprise deal drops precipitously.
To prevent session abandonment, organizations must deploy an Agent Escalation Middleware that monitors session execution states, detects boundary events, enriches the session context, and dispatches actionable alerts directly to technical sales teams inside Slack.
