Autonomous agents provide session callbacks, webhooks, or API polling mechanisms to surface state changes. When an agent enters a state such as REQUIRES_HUMAN_INTERVENTION, LIMIT_REACHED, or BLOCKED_ON_PERMISSIONS, the event listener catches the payload.
Key payload attributes to capture include:
session_id: The unique identifier for the running AI agent thread.
user_email / slack_user_id: The identity of the prospective buyer executing the agent.
repository_url: The target Git repository context.
last_action_prompt: The prompt or task the agent was attempting when it hit a barrier.
error_context: Structural diagnostic logs (e.g., HTTP 403, missing environment variable, ACU limit exceeded, unreachable network route).
session_workspace_url: Direct URL to Devin’s session workspace (including terminal outputs and file diffs).
Once the webhook payload lands in your API Gateway (Node.js/TypeScript, Python, or Go middleware), the service enriches the data before posting to Slack:
CRM Lookup: Query Salesforce, HubSpot, or Gong to map user_email to an existing Account, Opportunity stage, and assigned Technical Account Executive (TAE) or Solutions Architect (SA).
Context Compression: Summarize the agent's interaction history (using a fast LLM pass or structured log extraction) into a 3-bullet summary: What was attempted, Where it failed, and What entitlement is required.
Deep Link Generation: Generate direct URLs to the repository branch, the exact line of code, and the active Devin session workspace.
The following Node.js/TypeScript example demonstrates how to build a production-grade webhook handler that receives an escalation event from an AI agent platform, enriches the payload, and posts an interactive Slack message using Slack Block Kit.
import express, { Request, Response } from 'express';
import { WebClient } from '@slack/web-api';
import axios from 'axios';

const app = express();
app.use(express.json());

const slackClient = new WebClient(process.env.SLACK_BOT_TOKEN);
const CRM_API_ENDPOINT = process.env.CRM_API_ENDPOINT || 'https://api.crm.internal/v1';

interface AgentEscalationPayload {
  event_type: 'AGENT_BLOCKED' | 'ENTEPRISE_LIMIT_REACHED';
  session_id: string;
  user_email: string;
  repository_url: string;
  failure_reason: string;
  last_executed_command?: string;
  session_url: string;
  acu_used: number;
}

app.post('/api/v1/agent-escalation', async (req: Request, res: Response) => {
  try {
    const payload: AgentEscalationPayload = req.body;

    // 1. Validate incoming event
    if (payload.event_type !== 'ENTEPRISE_LIMIT_REACHED' && payload.event_type !== 'AGENT_BLOCKED') {
      return res.status(200).send('Event ignored');
    }

    // 2. Fetch CRM Account Context
    const crmData = await fetchCRMContext(payload.user_email);

    // 3. Construct Slack Block Kit Message
    const slackMessage = {
      channel: crmData.assigned_tae_slack_id || process.env.SLACK_FALLBACK_CHANNEL_ID!,
      text: `🚨 Enterprise Agent Escalation: ${crmData.account_name}`,
      blocks: [
        {
          type: "header",
          text: {
            type: "plain_text",
            text: "🚨 High-Intent AI Agent Escalation Captured",
            emoji: true
          }
        },
        {
          type: "section",
          fields: [
            {
              type: "mrkdwn",
              text: `*Account:* ${crmData.account_name}\n*User:* ${payload.user_email}`
            },
            {
              type: "mrkdwn",
              text: `*Opportunity Stage:* ${crmData.opp_stage}\n*ARR Potential:* $${crmData.arr_potential}`
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          type: "section",
          text: {
            type: "mrkdwn",
            text: `*Friction Point:* ${payload.failure_reason}\n*Target Repository:* <${payload.repository_url}|${payload.repository_url.split('/').slice(-2).join('/')}>`
          }
        },
        {
          type: "section",
          text: {
            type: "mrkdwn",
            text: `\`\`\`${payload.last_executed_command || 'Context: Enterprise network route or license gate hit.'}\`\`\``
          }
        },
        {
          type: "actions",
          elements: [
            {
              type: "button",
              text: {
                type: "plain_text",
                text: "🔍 Open Devin Session Workspace"
              },
              url: payload.session_url,
              style: "primary"
            },
            {
              type: "button",
              text: {
                type: "plain_text",
                text: "⚡ Grant Temporary ACUs / Outpost Access"
              },
              action_id: "grant_enterprise_access",
              value: JSON.stringify({ sessionId: payload.session_id, email: payload.user_email })
            },
            {
              type: "button",
              text: {
                type: "plain_text",
                text: "💬 Join User's Slack Thread"
              },
              action_id: "join_user_thread",
              style: "danger",
              value: payload.session_id
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    };

    // 4. Send Message via Slack Bot
    await slackClient.chat.postMessage(slackMessage);

    return res.status(200).json({ status: 'success', message: 'Escalation routed successfully.' });

  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Error handling agent escalation:', error);
    return res.status(500).send('Internal Server Error');
  }
});

async function fetchCRMContext(email: string) {
  try {
    const response = await axios.get(`${CRM_API_ENDPOINT}/lookup?email=${encodeURIComponent(email)}`);
    return response.data;
  } catch {
    // Fallback if CRM record is not found immediately
    return {
      account_name: "Unassigned / Product Led Lead",
      opp_stage: "Discovery",
      arr_potential: "50,000",
      assigned_tae_slack_id: null
    };
  }
}

app.listen(3000, () => console.log('Escalation Router running on port 3000'));

